        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with <strong class="text-white">6 rounds of 1 minute hard and 2 minutes easy</strong>,
            once a week, for three weeks. Set the pace for the final round rather than the first —
            the belt will not slow down for you the way the road does.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Progress by adding rounds, not speed. Keep the rest of your week
            <a href="/treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">genuinely easy</a>,
            because the interval session only works if the other sessions are not like it. Joints
            or neighbours a concern? Use incline intervals instead.
          </p>
        </div>
